WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.720
- It is nice to see you again!

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:02.684
- I know.

00:00:02.684 --> 00:00:03.517
- [Kelly] I got to see you in your room

00:00:03.517 --> 00:00:04.400
and I got to tell you I was
actually terrified that one time

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.233
you had to drive me around

00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:06.220
and you said I handled it well.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.887
- You played it so well I had no idea.

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:09.180
- -Kelly] That just means I'm a good liar.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.140
- You had glasses on too,
- -Kelly] I did.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.338
I had those, but yes.

00:00:12.338 --> 00:00:13.171
- Yeah, yeah

00:00:13.171 --> 00:00:14.180
- We look like babies.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.620
- We are babies. That's like '03 I heard.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.760
- [Kelly] I know, I don't even know

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.620
but I remember the hair,

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.750
it was definitely "My December" era.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.583
(audience laughing)

00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:22.416
Have ya'll met before?

00:00:22.416 --> 00:00:23.492
- We have not.
- No.

00:00:23.492 --> 00:00:24.900
- My pleasure.
- Yeah, my pleasure, yeah.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:25.980
- I've seen him

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:26.813
- Have you seen Hamilton?

00:00:26.813 --> 00:00:27.646
- I have, yeah

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:28.479
- Oh my Gosh! It was so good!

00:00:28.479 --> 00:00:29.580
- I have, my wife's a big fan as well,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.413
so are my children,

00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:32.540
so even my oldest daughter's been.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:33.373
- Wow!
- Yeah.

00:00:33.373 --> 00:00:35.660
- [Kelly] Yeah, look at that.
- I appreciate that.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.493
- I hope you didn't pay too much

00:00:36.493 --> 00:00:37.326
for your ticket.

00:00:37.326 --> 00:00:39.058
- We did, we were happy to.
(audience laughing)

00:00:39.058 --> 00:00:40.740
I mean, it was so good!

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.780
- Um, okay, this is a serious question.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.880
I love Talladega Nights (laughs)

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:45.713
- Who doesn't?

00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:46.546
- [Kelly] I love that film.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.410
Is it realistic?

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.520
Do not ruin my dreams.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.450
Go.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.440
- It is very close.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.090
Of course Hollywood's embellished some,

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.140
but yeah, I mean,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.550
if we can't laugh at ourself

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.270
as a sport, then we
shouldn't be out there.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.080
But I think they hit on quite

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.670
a few things that really do exist

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:00.900
in the world of NASCAR racing,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.080
I mean, we're rolling
billboard's out there

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.600
and just the play on all that

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.150
throughout the movie is fantastic.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.160
- Yeah, I love when I
go to a NASCAR event,

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.400
I mean the people watching,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.710
I love those people, those are my people.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:11.543
- World-class.

00:01:11.543 --> 00:01:13.320
- It's like those people are everybody,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.800
it's like everyone is so comfortable

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:15.800
in their skin,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.510
everybody is there for a party,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.360
it's like a country fest.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.193
- It is.

00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:21.026
- It's amazing.

00:01:21.026 --> 00:01:21.859
It's awesome, I love it.

00:01:21.859 --> 00:01:23.510
Well after seven championships,

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.870
you decided to retire this season, why?

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:26.703
- You know, I'm just looking

00:01:26.703 --> 00:01:28.100
for some balance,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.390
this is my 30th year

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:30.540
as a pro race-car driver,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.734
which is hard to say.
- Wow.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:32.567
(audience cheering)

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:33.400
- Thank you!

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.233
- That's a big career.

00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:36.430
- It's been an amazing run,

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.620
my 21st season in NASCAR

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.240
and then this year when it finishes up,

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.290
will be my 19th year

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.971
as the top-level driver, as a cup driver.

00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:44.804
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.637
- So, it's ya know

00:01:45.637 --> 00:01:46.470
I'm ready for some balance,

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.810
I'm not done working in racing,

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:48.840
I still have a lot of things

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:49.760
I want to accomplish

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.768
and really compete in some bucket-level

00:01:51.768 --> 00:01:53.590
ya know, races and events

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.160
and kind of check those boxes,

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.440
but two young children,

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.824
wonderful wife, life,

00:01:57.824 --> 00:01:59.920
all that stuff that,

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.470
I just wanna balance it out some.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.920
- [Kelly]] There's so
many things you love to do

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:03.753
but at the same time

00:02:03.753 --> 00:02:04.810
you don't wanna miss out on anything

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.400
especially when your kids are so young.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.970
'Cause they wanna play with you right now,

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.867
they don't once they
are a teenager. (laughs)

00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:11.345
(audience laughs)

00:02:11.345 --> 00:02:12.178
- True, that's very true,

00:02:12.178 --> 00:02:13.011
I had a moment last fall

00:02:13.011 --> 00:02:14.320
where just something shifted in my head

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.830
and it's never been about statistics

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:16.663
for me,

00:02:16.663 --> 00:02:17.810
and staying the course

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.200
would be for me to chase,

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.640
trying to win and eighth championship

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.473
more and more,
- Yeah.

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:22.450
And that's not what I'm about

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.670
and what I want to be about,

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.670
it's more about the journey

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:25.620
and the racing and the fun.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.360
So, once that shift happened in my mind,

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.410
I've been able to let go

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:30.760
and I'm really excited to see

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.810
what 21 brings.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.760
- [Kelly] That's so cool, man,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.593
I'll tell you what,

00:02:33.593 --> 00:02:34.823
you never know,

00:02:34.823 --> 00:02:35.656
I never knew I'd have this show,

00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:37.090
so you never know what your life has,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.200
you might have one, next year so.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.720
But you just had your final race

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.851
at your home track, right?

00:02:41.851 --> 00:02:42.684
- Correct.

00:02:42.684 --> 00:02:43.607
- Well how did you feel about that?

00:02:43.607 --> 00:02:44.700
Was it kind of emotional?

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.740
- Yeah very, very.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:46.890
Not only my home track,

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.590
but the place of my first win,

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:50.490
my family was up in the flag stand

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.470
waving the green flag,

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:53.380
they had me out in front

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.820
of the field leading everybody around

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:55.960
for this five-wide salute,

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:56.940
so highly emotional to say the least.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.810
- Wow! That's so cool.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.560
That's what I love about
that crowd too though.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.280
Everybody is so supportive,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.650
and there for everyone,

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.483
that's what I love about

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:05.904
that NAASCAR vibe, too.
- It is a big family.

00:03:05.904 --> 00:03:06.737
Every time I've gone,

00:03:06.737 --> 00:03:07.690
it's just a really big family, but

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:08.830
how does your wife handle

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:09.730
your dangerous career?

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.610
Because I know my brother-in-law

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.740
races ARA, and I'm just like, nah.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:14.573
I was like, I don't, yeah.

00:03:14.573 --> 00:03:15.779
- Yeah

00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:17.510
You know, educating her has been key,

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.000
we've been together 18 years

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.430
and that was right after,

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.880
when we first started dating,

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:22.713
was right after

00:03:22.713 --> 00:03:27.020
- It's a shame she's so ugly
(audience laughing)

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.210
It's a shame! (laughs)

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.200
- Dale Sr's tragic death happened

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.630
just after we started dating,

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.560
and she was able to learn

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.480
so much about crash dynamics

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.090
and the safety that followed

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:39.830
and then what I do to be
the more safe in the car,

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.520
that really educating her was

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.930
a big part of it all.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.130
And then my daughter's now

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.100
at the age where they're asking

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.260
those questions so I'm needing

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.360
to educate them too.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.390
- Are your daughter's like you?

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.690
Are they adrenaline junkies?

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.290
- They like to dabble, for sure.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.123
- [Kelly] Yeah?

00:03:52.123 --> 00:03:52.956
- Yeah, they're into it

00:03:52.956 --> 00:03:53.789
- [Kelly] Like what kind of things?

00:03:53.789 --> 00:03:55.330
- Ah we're in Colorado

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.163
a lot in the summer,

00:03:56.163 --> 00:03:58.960
so we're obviously in
the winter too, skiing.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.630
So skiing, hiking, mountain biking,

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.850
motocross riding,

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.830
I bought 'em some go-karts.
- Oh my gosh, they're so cool!

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.410
- Yeah, there's their go-kart's.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.037
- Yes!
- Their little rippers.

00:04:08.037 --> 00:04:09.670
Um, yeah, we have a lot of fun.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:10.503
There we are on the bikes.

00:04:10.503 --> 00:04:11.901
- Oh my gosh, that's adorable.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.270
Is that your wife?

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.103
- It is.

00:04:14.103 --> 00:04:14.936
She's on the left.

00:04:14.936 --> 00:04:16.674
- Could she be any hotter?

00:04:16.674 --> 00:04:18.086
(audience laughing)

00:04:18.086 --> 00:04:18.919
Geez!

00:04:18.919 --> 00:04:21.130
I'm like, leave some of it
- Oklahoma.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.511
for the rest of us!
- She's from Oklahoma.

00:04:22.511 --> 00:04:23.344
Oh, she's an Oklahoma girl?
- Yes.

00:04:23.344 --> 00:04:24.254
Oh my gosh!

00:04:24.254 --> 00:04:25.087
- Explains it all.

00:04:25.087 --> 00:04:25.920
- She's like I got this.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:26.753
Yeah.

00:04:26.753 --> 00:04:28.020
It's like a Texas woman, all right.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.330
Well what's the girliest thing you

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.440
have done with your girls?

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.957
Cause we have a lot of like,

00:04:31.957 --> 00:04:34.010
are they called "girl daddy's?",

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:35.100
I think that's what the term is.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.280
We've had a lot of them on this show

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.560
and I love that.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.660
- I'm involved in all levels

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.640
of what goes on,

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.610
but I'm under a lot of pressure

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.755
to have my toenails and
fingernails painted.

00:04:45.755 --> 00:04:46.588
(laughing)

00:04:46.588 --> 00:04:47.421
A lot of pressure.

00:04:47.421 --> 00:04:48.254
- They're wanting you to really

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:49.250
get into that?

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.083
- Yeah.

00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:50.916
- I will be honest,

00:04:50.916 --> 00:04:51.749
I've seen my husband paint

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:52.582
my daughter's toenails,

00:04:52.582 --> 00:04:53.415
our eldest,

00:04:53.415 --> 00:04:54.248
when we first got together,

00:04:54.248 --> 00:04:56.173
and he does a really good job.

00:04:56.173 --> 00:04:57.006
(audience laughing)

00:04:57.006 --> 00:04:57.890
Like better than me.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:59.130
- I've found out that I'm not bad

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.240
at braiding hair recently.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.438
- He's good at that too.

00:05:01.438 --> 00:05:02.470
Yeah, I don't know,

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.510
he had horses growing up,

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:04.940
so maybe cause he did
that with their mane?

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:05.917
I don't know.

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:06.940
- I'm terrible at it.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.550
- Oh, I can braid,

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.383
I played sports, so.

00:05:09.383 --> 00:05:10.590
- I'm really bad at the hair.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.350
I'm good at like the pretending,

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.200
so like the tea parties,

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.560
and like when I'm cast,

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.826
sometimes I'm step-mother or I'm,

00:05:19.826 --> 00:05:20.867
you know what I mean?
(laughing loudly)

00:05:20.867 --> 00:05:22.658
I'm good at the pretending stuff, yeah,

00:05:22.658 --> 00:05:24.470
but I'm not good at the hair braiding.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.303
- How many kids do you have?

00:05:25.303 --> 00:05:26.648
- Just one.

00:05:26.648 --> 00:05:27.481
One little girl.

00:05:27.481 --> 00:05:28.314
- How old?

00:05:28.314 --> 00:05:29.147
- She'll be three.

00:05:29.147 --> 00:05:29.980
- Three? Awesome. Congratulations.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.830
- Actually isn't her birthday April 23rd?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:32.663
- That's right.

00:05:32.663 --> 00:05:33.560
- A day before mine.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.469
- Get outta here!

00:05:34.469 --> 00:05:35.590
- She's gonna be amazing.
- Taurus. Taurus woman.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:36.477
- Yes! (laughing)

00:05:36.477 --> 00:05:37.725
- You'll let me know what I'm in for?

00:05:37.725 --> 00:05:39.034
Please tell me.
(audience laughing)

00:05:39.034 --> 00:05:39.867
- You know what?

00:05:39.867 --> 00:05:40.700
Buckle up! (laughing)

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.643
- Oh wow.

00:05:41.643 --> 00:05:42.476
(audience laughing)

00:05:42.476 --> 00:05:45.248
- We're sweet until we're not! (laughs)

00:05:45.248 --> 00:05:47.180
So do you ever let people drive you?

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.240
This is always my thought

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.730
with people that are race-car drivers,

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:50.563
do you not like,

00:05:50.563 --> 00:05:51.551
- No chance.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:52.384
- No chance? (laughs)

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:53.217
- Yeah, no chance.

00:05:53.217 --> 00:05:54.280
I mean, for one,

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.387
- Does your wife remember
how to drive? (laughs)

00:05:56.387 --> 00:05:57.980
- She's the most cautious driver

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:58.940
which drives me crazy,

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.950
so no chance I'll let her drive.

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:02.090
But yeah, control freak,

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:02.923
I'll admit it

00:06:02.923 --> 00:06:04.360
but the other thing that you're going

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.193
to find funny

00:06:05.193 --> 00:06:07.540
is I get motion sickness really easily.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.828
- So if you don't drive,

00:06:08.828 --> 00:06:10.210
no, this happened to me
- It's awful.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.230
when I was pregnant so I

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:12.490
was just vomiting all the time,

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.533
it was wonderful,

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.430
and I literally would not

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.510
let anyone drive

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.343
and they're like

00:06:18.343 --> 00:06:19.176
"well what if you vomit at the wheel,"

00:06:19.176 --> 00:06:20.298
I'm like, I got a bag

00:06:20.298 --> 00:06:22.010
because if I'm in that seat,

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:23.447
I get so motion sickness.
- So bad, yeah.

00:06:23.447 --> 00:06:24.650
But if you're in control,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.483
you're not.

00:06:25.483 --> 00:06:26.316
That's so true.

00:06:26.316 --> 00:06:27.220
- Yep, if I'm driving the vehicle,

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.053
I'm fine,

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:29.270
now if you put me in a cab or something

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.170
in New York,

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:31.003
it's awful.

00:06:31.003 --> 00:06:32.391
- Oh, all the turns
- Yes it's terrible

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.120
- Just all those roads

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.270
they're just like crazy.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.541
- They're great drivers, by the way.

00:06:36.541 --> 00:06:37.374
- And everybody's honking.

00:06:37.374 --> 00:06:38.207
Do what?

00:06:38.207 --> 00:06:39.040
- Those taxi drivers in New York

